.TH EVERY 1.SH NAMEevery \- run a program at intervals.SH SYNOPSIS\fBevery\fRseconds program [arguments].SH DESCRIPTION\fBevery\fRforks\fIprogram\fRwith its\fIarguments\fRevery\fIseconds\fRseconds, until you stop it.  The program is found as a module or alongthe execution path; when it cannot be forked\fBevery\fRsays so, with the error number:\fBcan't fork date, error 221\fR.\fR.SH EXAMPLES.nfevery 60 free /h0 &       report free space every minute.fi.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOrepeat, cron